--TEST--
A write to a `Throwable`'s `readonly` property through a `mixed` receiver throws, and the message stays as the constructor wrote it — `rule:classes/readonly-is-written-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Renamer {
    public static function rename(mixed $error): void {
        $error->message = "b";
    }
}

RuntimeError $e = new RuntimeError("a");
try {
    Renamer::rename($e);
} catch (RuntimeError $failure) {
    echo $failure->message, "\n";
}
echo $e->message, "\n";
--EXPECT--
cannot modify `readonly` property `RuntimeError::$message`
a
